<title>FRANCE: EU clears over 600,000 T flour exports.</title>
<headline>EU clears over 600,000 T flour exports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union granted over the past two weeks licences to export over 600,000 tonnes of flour, member-country officials said on Friday.</p>
<p>Between February 7 and February 13 the EU cleared sales of 569,700 tonnes of EU soft wheat with licences carrying a 26.00 Ecus refund, they said.</p>
<p>Between February 14 and February 20 the EU granted licences to export 40,000 tonnes of EU flour at a refund of 24.50 Ecus per tonne.  </p>
<p>On Thursday the EU reduced the flour refund to 20.00 Ecus per tonne from a previous level of 24.50 Ecus, in line with a cut in the export refund for wheat grain.</p>
<p>EU flour exports between July 1, 1996 and February 18, 1997, reached 4.7 million tonnes tonnes (grain equivalent) against 3.5 million at the same time last year, officials also said.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
